<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · mountain</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ezhimala</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Mount Eli, Ezhimalai</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ezhimala is a coastal hill in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kannur">Kannur</a> district of northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kerala">Kerala</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, rising from the shore of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arabian-sea">Arabian Sea</a>. In Sangam poetry it was the seat of the chief <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nannan">Nannan</a>, and it later gave its name to the Mushika kingdom of northern Kerala, from which the Kolathiri rulers claimed descent. It is now the site of the Indian Naval Academy.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ezhimala.jpg" alt="Ezhimala" width="320" height="212" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sreejithk2000 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ezhimala_beach.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
